msgid "LightWare GRF250 / GRF500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:7
#: 0a12cd8154824c508cbb0e8947ef4fc5
msgid "The `LightWare GRF250 <https://lightwarelidar.com/shop/grf-250/>`__ and `GRF500 <https://lightwarelidar.com/shop/grf-500/>`__ are long-range lidar-based rangefinders. Both models support serial (UART) communication and provide accurate distance and signal-strength data at configurable update rates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:10
#: da79ff7a64e84e57953dcee56b9923ab
msgid "GRF250: 0.2 m – 250 m range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:11
#: 4e48509cb045473b89538ea602d5a7b5
msgid "GRF500: 0.2 m – 500 m range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:18
#: 825a171689cd4b808d31a17e7fc14520
msgid "Support for the LightWare GRF250 and GRF500 sensors was added in ArduPilot 4.7 and later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:21
#: bcc7455668274537a98f646e436c70bf
msgid "Serial Connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:23
#: 801567fe533c4fb99abd8acdfe21ee51
msgid "The GRF sensors communicate via UART using 3.3 V or 5 V logic levels. Connect the TX of the Lidar to the RX of the autopilot UART port, and the RX of the Lidar to the TX of the same port. Also connect GND and 5 V to power the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:31
#: 6ee931871f364db39f672ea80a3a38be
msgid "Example (SERIAL4):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:33
#: 1d41e805782d48b9b867dcce8b63044b
msgid "If the GRF is connected to the autopilots' SERIAL4 port and it is the first rangefinder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:35
#: 9d5f3cb048174296a979d0f3c7f2021c
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 9 (Lidar)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:36
#: 235bfe003ba6447580a8dc4988729ba7
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL4_BAUD <SERIAL4_BAUD>` = 115 (115200 baud)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:37
#: 5af3cef6ac9e4025ba058c1ac89eba27
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 45 (LightWareGRF)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:38
#: ee02888c233a4f2eafe53882b854105d
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_SCALING <RNGFND1_SCALING>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:39
#: 240e414a67bd440dade3da51af40344f
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MIN <RNGFND1_MIN>` = 0.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:40
#: 6b4549bb8fb44f7f8f3385927d74d5ed
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX <RNGFND1_MAX>` = 250 *(for GRF250)* or 500 *(for GRF500)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:42
#: b35c8b24c6ba4dba993cf285f2a613fc
msgid "If instead you are using the SERIAL2 port, set :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 9 and :ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 115."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:44
#: 85d85a0358e845a5b0a64e96edfc083e
msgid "Power note: The GRF sensors can draw higher current than typical serial peripherals. Check your flight controller’s 5 V peripheral rail limits — an external 5 V supply may be required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:49
#: 348e6ceb48e34d34b9547f4fac5932e6
msgid "Additional GRF-specific Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:51
#: f6eaf5d2d13b47afa1159b1b1ab94ccd
msgid "When :ref:`RNGFNDx_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` is set to 45 (LightWareGRF), the Serial port protocol is set to 9, and the autopilot is rebooted, the following additional parameters become available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:53
#: a257197c9d584912b0ebd825484c5857
msgid ":ref:`RNGFNDx_GRF_RET <RNGFND1_GRF_RET>`: Selects which return type to use (0: FirstRaw, 1: FirstFiltered, 2: LastRaw, 3: LastFiltered)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:54
#: ba82235746c744779209c089335a8691
msgid ":ref:`RNGFNDx_GRF_ST <RNGFND1_GRF_ST>`: Sets the minimum acceptable return signal strength in dB. Returns weaker than this value are ignored (0 disables filtering)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:55
#: 8f45f27809f84526b8a375f00df7f002
msgid ":ref:`RNGFNDx_GRF_RATE <RNGFND1_GRF_RATE>`: Sets the sensor update rate in Hz. GRF250 supports 1–50 readings per second, while GRF500 supports 0.5–10 readings per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-grf250-lidar.rst:58
